            "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load vectors and cast to float64 for precision during distance computation\n    X = np.load(\"vectors_secondary.npy\").astype(np.float64)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    batch_size = 1000\n\n    for start in range(0, n, batch_size):\n        end = min(start + batch_size, n)\n        X_batch = X[start:end]\n        norms_batch = sq_norms[start:end]\n\n        # Intra-batch pairs (diagonal block)\n        G_diag = X_batch @ X_batch.T\n        D2_diag = norms_batch[:, None] + norms_batch[None, :] - 2.0 * G_diag\n        np.maximum(D2_diag, 0.0, out=D2_diag)\n        np.fill_diagonal(D2_diag, 0.0)\n        total += float(np.sum(np.sqrt(D2_diag)))\n\n        # Inter-batch pairs with remaining rows (off-diagonal blocks)\n        if end < n:\n            X_rest = X[end:]\n            norms_rest = sq_norms[end:]\n            G_rest = X_batch @ X_rest.T\n            D2_rest = norms_batch[:, None] + norms_rest[None, :] - 2.0 * G_rest\n            np.maximum(D2_rest, 0.0, out=D2_rest)\n            # Factor of 2 accounts for both ordered pairs (i, j) and (j, i)\n            total += 2.0 * float(np.sum(np.sqrt(D2_rest)))\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
